  "description": "Tree Description:\rSingle mature broadleaf tree (likely plane or similar species) located adjacent to a boundary wall at the rear/side of the property.\r\rProposed Works:\rFell tree to ground level.\rStump to be treated with eco-plugs or herbicide to prevent regrowth.\r\rReason for Works:\rThe tree is in close proximity to a masonry boundary wall and is exhibiting structural and physiological concerns. Visual inspection shows:\r\r* Evidence of historic wounds and poor occlusion on the main stem\r* Areas of bark dysfunction and possible underlying decay\r* Included unions and dense upper crown structure creating sail effect\r* Close proximity to the wall, with potential for root-related damage and structural pressure\r\rDue to these factors, the tree presents a potential risk of structural failure, which could result in damage to the boundary wall and surrounding property.\r\rGiven the tree?s condition and location, removal is considered the most appropriate management option to mitigate risk.",
